body:
Hi @daveiglu

Indeed from the InstantSearch perspective there is only the `render` event. Underneath, however there are other events managed by the [JS Helper](https://community.algolia.com/algoliasearch-helper-js/). For example, there is [an event where new results](https://community.algolia.com/algoliasearch-helper-js/reference.html#AlgoliaSearchHelper#event:result) are received:

```js
// after search.start() has been called
search.helper.on('result', (results, state) => {
  // results contains the actual results
  // state contains the state used to generate those results
});
```
